    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 1752 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaungpaya">Alaungpaya</a>, a village headman who reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> within a few years and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Rangoon</a>.</li><li>Its armies destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in 1767, repelled four Qing invasions and conquered Arakan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> and Manipur.</li><li>Three wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, in 1824–1826, 1852 and 1885, stripped it of territory and ended in annexation.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindon-min">Mindon</a>’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuthodaw-pagoda">Kuthodaw Pagoda</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandalay">Mandalay</a> the entire Pali Buddhist canon is carved on 729 marble slabs, each housed in its own small shrine.</p></aside>
    </section>

